Z||000000||Philphine||06-29-2001||10:30 AM||||<BR>two weeks (off and on)<P>four different bleeding methods (including buying two different bleeding kits, a one man and a mityvac. also a three man with one constanly pouring in fluid one pumping the clutch and one opening and closing the bleeder. i ended up jacking up the front and letting it gravity bleed.)<P>new master and slave cylinders (replacing ones i just got about a year and a half ago)<P>that was all it took to get me back on the road. i went back and looked at some old threads and saw were most recommended getting original gm parts, so since the last ones i got weren't and i wasn't getting anywhere trying to bleed the system i went ahead and got new gm cylinders. i replaced the master first 'cause i saw a little seeping around the shaft inside the car. it still wouldn't bleed so after reading about the cast cylinders not being as good i replaced the slave too.<P>i got the one man bleeder kit 'cause they work good when i do brakes. i was going to try to do it at work and ended up losing the little clutch acton i had. thats when my supervisor and the shift mechanic came out and it became a 3 man operation, it got worse. i ended up jamming gears to get home. i got the mityvac after getting the master cyl. and still wasn't able to bleed it. at that point i jacked up the front and let it gravity bleed. i actually got a little clutch action back but not enough to drive. back to the dealer to get the slave cyl. got it on, went strait to a gravity bleed that time and i'm driving again.<P>i love a simple repair. <P>------------------<BR>Phil T<P>'87 coupe (feral)<BR>'84 indy<BR>'84 coupe (cheap thrill)<BR>'84 chop top (project. or at least an interesting collection of parts)||||reg||1
Z||000001||ROB MAC||06-29-2001||11:54 AM||||The only way it would work for me was- Push pedal THEN crack the bleeder- close it and release pedal.Repeat many times. After the bubbles are gone remove bleeder screw and pullback the slave pushrod and replace screw. I used a broom handle to depress pedal. I recommend a second person.||||reg||1
